})
</code></pre>

Aspect Description Purpose HTTP orchestrator — a thin layer between the network and the business domain Internal role Accepts an <code>HttpRequest</code>, calls serializer → service/selector, returns an <code>HttpResponse</code> In the request lifecycle Parses the request, delegates logic, formats the response Can return HTML, JSON, PDF, CSV, Redirect <p>Mental model: A dispatcher — takes the call, connects it to the right specialist and passes the answer back. It decides nothing on its own.</p> <pre><code># A view in clean architecture — as thin as possible
class FloodEventCreateAPIView(APIView):

    def post(self, request):
        serializer = FloodEventInputSerializer(data=request.data)  # validation
        serializer.is_valid(raise_exception=True)

        event = flood_event_create(**serializer.validated_data)    # business logic in a service

        return Response(FloodEventOutputSerializer(event).data, status=201)
</code></pre> A view must NOT A view MUST ❌ contain SQL or ORM queries ✅ validate via an <code>InputSerializer</code> ❌ contain business logic ✅ call a <code>service</code> (mutations) ❌ orchestrate transactions ✅ call a <code>selector</code> (reads) ❌ compute or transform data ✅ format via an <code>OutputSerializer</code> ❌ know about Celery tasks directly ✅ return a <code>Response</code> <p>Mistake in the standard architecture: <code>views.py</code> is described as the place for "business logic". In clean/production architecture, a view is only the HTTP layer. All the logic lives in <code>services.py</code> and <code>selectors.py</code>.</p>

Feature SQLite PostgreSQL Data types limited full (JSONB, ARRAY, UUID, hstore) Concurrency 1 writer at a time full MVCC, many writers Full-text search basic tsvector, GIN indexes CheckConstraint supported supported Size a file on disk server, network Backup <code>cp db.sqlite3</code> <code>pg_dump</code>, WAL <p>In notes_chat_app: <code>settings.py</code> automatically selects the DB from <code>DATABASE_URL</code>:</p> <pre><code># notes_project/settings.py
import dj_database_url

DATABASES = {
    'default': dj_database_url.config(
        default='sqlite:///db.sqlite3',  # fallback for tests without Docker
        conn_max_age=0,                  # IMPORTANT for ASGI: do not keep connections between requests
    )
}
</code></pre> <p><code>conn_max_age=0</code> is critical for ASGI/async. Persistent connections are not thread-safe in an async context.</p>

